@mattpap Notice the `ui-datepicker-div` below.  Does this need to be inside of `bk-root`?
<img width="755" alt="screen shot 2016-06-01 at 3 12 39 pm" src="https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/433221/15725233/8cf6886a-2810-11e6-8921-54271e8b65ac.png">

I chatted with @canavandl who mentioned this issue is that `datepicker` is being instantiated without running through `build_views`.  I was going to import the jQueryUiPrefixer and simply but looks saw a note in that it may not be there in the future. https://github.com/bokeh/bokeh/blob/master/bokehjs/src/coffee/common/build_views.coffee#L51-L52

@brendan, @bryevdv - it's not that.

If you add a style sheet that also has `ui-widget-header` along with the `bk-ui-widget-header` etc. then the styling will work I believe.

The datepicker is initially initialized with the bk- prefixes but then it seems to re-initialize itself and remove the bk- prefixes. I'll try and work up a patch tomorrow.

@birdsarah just to be clear, with patch above, that attaches the date picker to an `input` (which seems much better) it does not even ever get initialized to `bk-`prefixed. 

Edit: patch here:

https://github.com/bokeh/bokeh/issues/4204#issuecomment-222186937

@bryevdv, I have an email from you that says:

> I'll also add that adding the bk- prefix to all the divs and classes the date picker creates, by hand in the browser, has no effect. 

I can't see that comment. But if that's still true, it's definitely surprising, and I'll look into it tomorrow.
